  [heading level=2 fg=yellow]Nesting and wrapping[/heading]
  [text]Inline spans nest, so a sentence can carry [text bold]emphasis[/text] and
  [text fg=cyan]colour[/text] without leaving the paragraph. Long paragraphs wrap
  at the region width rather than at the terminal edge, which is what makes a
  narrow column readable next to a wide one.[/text]
